														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1295470">
									

<p>Yet more proof that the Imperial system is superior to the metric system. Try to confuse &quot;in&quot; with &quot;ft&quot; some time&#8230;</p>
<p>^_^ Actually, there is some grain of truth in that. Redundancy in languages serves a purpose. Having two letters helps to ensure that a one-letter error shows up as error (here, confusing m with M) rather than as new meaning. It's one of the reasons that Heinlein's Speedtalk is implausible.</p>

							</div>

								
					
