					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drewbear" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301632); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=301632&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608498501" alt="Drewbear" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=301632)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drewbear" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(301632); return false;" >Drewbear</a></span> <span class="odate time_1340974469 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">29 Jun 2012 12:54</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1494012">
									

<p>Actually, I got to agree with the Kelvin thing. I just did some quick googling and while it's perfectly possible to refrigerate something below 3&#160;K, the current lower bound is somewhere around 1&#160;K, and even that takes considerable effort. Maybe change it to 5&#160;K instead of 0.5&#160;K?</p>
<p>That being said, I can see Severe being blase about the temperature thing; it's part of the standard containment protocols for this beastie and was where it was supposed to be at, so why should he get excited about it?</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Giving bearhugs to the unsuspecting since 1872.</p>

